EXPERIMENT, out of series, DOES NOT WORK -- kept for the next attempt.

misc: decd: program the source route from the submitted descriptor

Goal: move the DECD source route out of shell and into the driver -- seven
geometry words, source enable, two-plane format byte, config commit, all
derived from the descriptor.  auto_route defaults to 0 because the result is
WRONG ON THE PANEL.

WHAT IT DOES CORRECTLY.  With auto_route=1 and no shell writes to the AFBD
block, one submit takes the block from all-zero to exactly the hand-verified
state, and logs it:

  0x05600010 = 0x03000313   enable + format 3
  0x05600020 = 0x02CF04FF   crop 1280x720
  0x05600030 = 0x02D00500   picture
  0x05600040 = 0x00000500   stride
  0x0560004c = 0x01680500   chroma
  0x05600011 = 0x03         two-plane format byte
  decd 5600000.dec: DECD route: 1280x720 stride 1280 hw-format 3

WHAT IS WRONG.  The panel shows the frame DOUBLED side by side, filling only
the top half, with teal/shifted colour (local/lcd-photos/test_81).  That is the
signature of a 2-bytes-per-pixel fetch: each display row consumes two source
rows, so even rows land left, odd rows right, and 720 rows run out at display
row 360.

THE HARD PART, recorded so the next attempt does not repeat it: a full
0x05600000..0x1FF dump of a working run (shell route) and a broken one (driver
route) is BYTE-IDENTICAL across every configuration register.  Only live
counters and two timing values differ:

  0x05600058  good=0x46  driver=0x45
  0x0560005c  good=0x3B  driver=0x3A
  0x05600184  good=0x3A  driver=0x4C

Identical final state with different output means the fault is in the SEQUENCE
or the moment of latching, not the values.  A register dump cannot see it.
Whatever 0x05600014 samples at commit time is not fully described by the
registers we know about.

THINGS TRIED, all still doubled:
  - reordering so the source disable and IOMMU flip happen before the submit,
    leaving the driver's route as the last word
  - re-applying the route when the source enable bits are clear, not only when
    the geometry changes (caching on geometry alone silently skipped the route
    on every run after the first)
  - publishing plane addresses via 0x0560006c in both modes (the harness was
    writing the four ring slots and never publishing them)

NEXT IDEAS, untried: have the driver also write the plane addresses and the
0x6c publish itself rather than splitting ownership with the harness; or trace
the exact write order of a working shell run and replay it verbatim from the
driver, including the reads, since a read may be part of the latch behaviour.

item->format_shadow was hardcoded to 0 (= RGB888), which is why every trace
reported format 0 while the panel was fed NV12.  It now comes from fmt_attr_tbl
column 8.  That part is correct and independent of the failure above.

DELIBERATELY NOT INCLUDED: chroma gain 0x05140508 and plane selector
0x051c006c.  They live in the display engine, are not mapped by this driver,
and are shared with the MIPS logo path.

THE SHELL PATH STILL WORKS: tools/video/decd-all-preconditions.sh with
DRIVER_ROUTE unset renders correctly in all three modes, including real Cedrus
playback.  Nothing here is load-bearing for that result.

